+# Aegis — Edge / Offline & Safety Patterns
+
+This patch implements:
+- Edge-first local Milvus cache and a sync agent for delayed sync to central Milvus.
+- Pre-provisioned fetch-tokens for emergency A2A approvals (fetchtoken service).
+- Staged autonomy controller that enforces observe → recommend → auto flows and ties to A2A when required.
+- Gatekeeper data region constraint to enforce regional partitioning metadata.
+- Quick takedown API for urgent privacy/legal deletion requests.
+- Retriever curation job for freshness checks + MCP alerts.
+- PREEMPT_RT cold validation workflow template.
+
+Deployment hints:
+- Edge: deploy `local_milvus_compose.yml` on the edge box. Edge ingestion must write evidence files to /data/sync_queue as JSON for the sync agent.
+- Sync: run `services/edge/milvus_sync.py` on the edge; configure CENTRAL_MILVUS_HOST and collection name.
+- Fetchtokens: create a small number of tokens via `POST /admin/create` with short expiry (store token JSON encrypted offline). Redeem/verify via /verify on approver side.
+- Staged autonomy: wire verifier to call `/decide` on `staged_autonomy_controller` instead of directly invoking sandbox actions.
+- PREEMPT_RT validation: provision self-hosted runners with PREEMPT_RT images and run the `preempt_rt_cold_validation` workflow for lab validation (cold chamber if available).
+- Privacy & GDPR: ensure ingestion pipelines call Presidio adapter and that originals are encrypted with KMS. Use takedown API to quickly queue deletion requests and run operator process to clear artifacts.
+
+Operational checks:
+- Periodic sync success rate and queue depth monitored (edge).
+- Fetchtoken list rotation and audit in MCP.
+- curation job alert thresholds tuned (STALE_DAYS, STALE_PCT_THRESHOLD).
+- Ensure HIL evidence signing + FMEA link exists before enabling auto-actuation in production.
+
